\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Saviour, again to Thy dear name 
\par we raise
\par With one accord our parting hymns
\par of praise;
\par We stand to bless Thee ere our 
\par worship cease,
\par Then, lowly kneeling, wait Thy 
\par word of peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Grant us Thy peace  upon our 
\par homeward way;
\par With Thee began, with Thee shall 
\par end the day;
\par Guard Thou the lips from sin, the
\par hearts from shame,
\par That in this house have called upon
\par Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Grant us Thy peace, Lord, through
\par the coming night,
\par Turn Thou for us its darkness into 
\par light;
\par From harm and danger keep Thy 
\par children free,
\par For dark and light are both alike 
\par to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Grant us Thy peace throughout
\par our earthly life,
\par Our balm in sorrow, and our stay
\par in strife;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Then, when Thy voice shall bid 
\par our conflict cease,
\par Call us, O Lord, o Thine eternal
\par peace.
\par              Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

